---
source: crates/pse-host/src/cli.rs
expression: "format!(\"-h\\n{short}\\n--help\\n{long}\")"
---
-h
Attempt every independent Just recipe under one native foreground owner

Usage: pse run-all [OPTIONS] <RECIPES>...

Arguments:
  <RECIPES>...  Independent zero-argument Just recipes; every recipe is attempted in order

Options:
  -C <checkout>
      --justfile <JUSTFILE>  Native Just file; relative paths are resolved from the selected checkout
      --format <FORMAT>      Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations [env: PSE_FORMAT] [default: auto] [possible values: auto, human, json, ndjson]
      --session <SESSION>    Associate this bundle and its children with an explicit agent session
      --fields <FIELDS>      Select comma-separated literal top-level payload names (for example records). Dots and slashes do not navigate nested data; schema shows valid choices
      --budget <BUDGET>      Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts
  -h, --help                 Print help (see more with '--help')
--help
Attempt every independent Just recipe under one native foreground owner

Usage: pse run-all [OPTIONS] <RECIPES>...

Arguments:
  <RECIPES>...
          Independent zero-argument Just recipes; every recipe is attempted in order

Options:
  -C <checkout>


      --justfile <JUSTFILE>
          Native Just file; relative paths are resolved from the selected checkout

      --format <FORMAT>
          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Human for a terminal, JSON for pipes
          - human:  Concise summary and pretty structured detail
          - json:   One JSON envelope
          - ndjson: Compact normalized records followed by an observation summary

          [env: PSE_FORMAT]
          [default: auto]

      --session <SESSION>
          Associate this bundle and its children with an explicit agent session

      --fields <FIELDS>
          Select comma-separated literal top-level payload names (for example records). Dots and slashes do not navigate nested data; schema shows valid choices

      --budget <BUDGET>
          Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
